cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. If you use results derived from the TCIA
  datasets it analyses, also cite those datasets and the TCIA repository paper (see references).
title: "DoseShift Explorer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shahbazi
    given-names: Sobhan
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/callmesobhan/doseshift-explorer"
abstract: >-
  Research tool for exploring how controlled geometric perturbations (setup shifts, rotations,
  deformation) and dose-grid alignment assumptions (voxel centre vs corner, resolution,
  interpolation, structure sampling) change DVHs and plan-quality metrics in radiotherapy.
  Not for clinical use.
keywords:
  - radiotherapy
  - DVH
  - DICOM-RT
  - dose robustness
  - Monte Carlo
  - medical physics
